This drawer contains Amiga-specific helpers used while maintaining the
AmigaPython port (docs, local tests, experimental modules, and legacy
utilities).

AmigaPython 2.7.18 notes:
- Module documentation lives in Docs/ (mirrored under Python/docs/amiga
  in the distribution tree).
- Prefer the builtin `amiga' module for Dos helpers, ASL/catalog/icon,
  EasyRequest/CurrentTime/DisplayBeep, AvailMem, and path converters.
- Prefer builtin `amigagui' for simple Intuition windows (plot/line).
- Secondary raw LVO FFI: builtin `amigalibs' + Tools/ConvertFD.py +
  Lib/site-python/*lib.py (see intuitionlib.py). Not for general apps.
- Site-specific Python modules belong under Lib/site-python (or the
  versioned site-packages path for your install).

Drawers:
  Docs/                  Amiga module and port documentation
  Diffs/                 Output area for mkdiffs.py against stock sources
  testset/               Extra Amiga-oriented test scripts (also in AmigaTests)
  experimental_modules/  Historic simplegfx/Execlib sources (shipped as
                         amigagui / amiga.AvailMem in the main build)
  unused/                Historic ConvertFD/amigalibs/intuitionlib snapshots
  test/                  Legacy Setup/config fragments

See the project README / BUILD docs for how the 2.7.18 interpreter is built.
